  "response_text": "Handling an unsafe situation at home can be a stressful and challenging experience. Here are some steps you can take to ensure your safety and the safety of others:\n\n1. Assess the situation: Take a moment to assess the situation and identify the potential risks. Determine what is causing the danger and what immediate actions can be taken to mitigate the risk.\n\n2. Evacuate the area: If possible, evacuate the area immediately. Follow the instructions of any emergency personnel and leave the area as quickly and safely as possible.\n\n3. Call for help: If you are unable to evacuate the area, call for help immediately. This may include calling 911 or contacting local emergency services.\n\n4. Secure the area: If you are unable to evacuate the area, try to secure the area as much as possible. This may include turning off utilities, closing doors and windows, and covering any exposed areas.\n\n5. Stay calm: It is important to stay calm and composed during an emergency. This will help you make better decisions and avoid panic.\n\n6. Follow instructions: Follow any instructions given by emergency personnel or other authority figures. This may include wearing a mask, using a gas mask, or following specific safety protocols.\n\n7. Seek medical attention: If you or someone else is injured, seek medical attention immediately. Do not delay in seeking help.\n\nRemember, it is important to take immediate safety priorities into account when dealing with an unsafe situation at home. By taking these steps, you can help ensure your safety and the safety of others.",
